# text = The estate of Dale of Allington had been coterminous with the parish of Allington for some hundreds of years ; and though , as I have said , the race of squires had possessed nothing of superhuman discretion , and had perhaps been guided in their walks through life by no very distinct principles , still there had been with them so much of adherence to a sacred law , that no acre of the property had ever been parted from the hands of the existing squire .
