# text = They had been obstinate men ; believing much in themselves ; just according to their ideas of justice ; hard to their tenants -- but not known to be hard even by the tenants themselves , for the rules followed had ever been the rules on the Allington estate ; imperious to their wives and children , but imperious within bounds , so that no Mrs Dale had fled from her lord's roof , and no loud scandals had existed between father and sons ; exacting in their ideas as to money , expecting that they were to receive much and to give little , and yet not thought to be mean , for they paid their way , and gave money in parish charity and in county charity .
