# text = I am inclined to say that Adolphus Crosbie was not a mere clerk ; and I do not think that he would have been so called , even by Lily Dale , had he not given signs to her that he was a Now a man in becoming a swell -- a swell of such an order as could possibly be known to Lily Dale -- must have ceased to be a mere clerk in that very process .
