# text = She had learned that Mrs Cradell , the widow of a barrister , who had also succeeded in getting her son into the Income-tax Office , had placed him in charge of Mrs Roper ; and she , with many injunctions to that motherly woman , submitted her own boy to the same custody Mrs Eames had said to Mrs Roper Mrs Roper had answered , conscientiously asked the mother , very anxious in her heart as to this new life in which her boy was to be left to follow in so many things the guidance of his own lights Mrs Roper promised accordingly , and Johnny Eames was left under her charge .
