# text = He was a man who had been much given to royal visitings and attendances , to parties in the Highlands , to -- no doubt necessary -- prolongations of the London season , to sojournings at certain German watering-places , convenient , probably , in order that he might study the ways and ceremonies of German Courts -- and to various other absences from home , occasioned by a close pursuit of his own special aims in life ; for the Earl de Courcy had been a great courtier .
