# text = As he sat in his easy-chair after dinner he hardly winked above once or twice ; and when he had taken the large bowl of tea , which he usually swallowed in a semi-somnolent condition , he was quite lively he said , jumping up and rubbing his eyes Whereupon Dr Crofts explained that Mr Crosbie was engaged to Lilian Dale said Crafts said Crofts Dr Crofts didn't exactly see the matter in this light , but he was not anxious to argue it very closely with the earl he said Soon after this , Crofts took his horse and rode home , having promised the earl that he would dine with him again before long said the earl
