# text = He expected every guest who sat there to be dressed in such guise as the fashion of the day demanded ; and he himself , though his morning costume was by no means brilliant , never dined , even when alone , without having put himself into a suit of black , with a white cravat , and having exchanged the old silver hunting-watch which he carried during the day tied round his neck by a bit of old ribbon , for a small gold watch , with a chain and seals , which in the evening always dangled over his waistcoat .
