# text = Crosbie , as he wrote them , conceived that they would in some way prepare the poor girl for the coming blow -- that they would , at any rate , make her know that all was not right ; but in so supposing he had not counted on the constancy of her nature , nor had he thought of the promise which , she had given him that nothing should make her doubt him .
