# text = For all this he would take no fee -- nor had he ever taken a fee from Mrs Dale Bell said to him one evening , as he stood with her at the drawing-room fire , after he had left the patient's room On that day Lily was over the worst of the fever , and he had been able to tell Mrs Dale that he did not think that she was now in danger he said said the doctor , laughing Then , instead of going , he sat himself down he said Bell now had also sat down , and they both remained for some time looking at the fire in silence he said , at last she said
