# text = Eames made a little , attempt at leaving the room , but he was implored by Lupex with such earnest protestations of friendship to remain , and was so weakly fearful of being charged with giving himself airs , that he did as he was desired said Lupex , raising to his mouth a steaming goblet of gin-and-water , and wishing you many years to enjoy your official prosperity said Eames said Cradell Whereupon Mr Lupex finished his first measure of gin-and-water continued Lupex ; and , though he did not at once go to work boldly at the mixing of another glass of toddy , he began gradually , and as if by instinct , to finger the things which would be necessary for that operation said Eames
