# text = As Mrs Dale did not answer him at once , Lily spoke said Hopkins said Mrs Dale , using the same argument by which Eames had endeavoured to excuse his departure to Mrs Roper said Lily This , which Hopkins spoke in the excitement of the moment , was perfectly unintelligible to Lily , and Mrs Dale , who shuddered as she heard him , said not a word to call for any explanation continued Hopkins said Mrs Dale said Mrs Dale said Mrs Dale and Hopkins , as he spoke , indicated by a motion of his head that he was making reference to the squire said Lily said Lily exclaimed Mrs Dale , as soon as Hopkins had taken himself off Mrs Dale did not answer her daughter at once , fearing to commit herself by words which could not be retracted .
