# text = The door was opened for him by the faithful Jemima and the poor girl , who had always taken his side in the adventures of the lodging-house , raised her hands on high and lamented the fate which had separated her favourite from its fortunes . " I suppose you knows it all , Mister Johnny ? " Mister Johnny said that he believed he did know it all , and asked for the mistress of the house So upstairs into the drawing-room he went , and there he found the mother and daughter , and with them Miss Spruce , tightly packed up in her bonnet and shawl Amelia was saying said Mrs Roper , sobbing It struck Eames immediately that , though he had been an inmate in the house for two years , he had never before heard that maiden lady's Christian name .
