# text = This work of unpacking and resettling was not yet over , when the battle of the manure broke out , and therefore it was that Hopkins , when his feelings had become altogether too much for him came at last to Lily , and laying down at her feet all the weight and all the glory of his sixty odd years of life , implored her to make matters straight for him Then Hopkins turned away and wept said Lily , creeping close up against his chair said Lily In answer to this , Lily of course promised that she would come and help said she said the squire
